LOG
Diagnostic on Grok & Perplexity Nodes
Perplexity (perplexity.ai): It printed its response block, but missed closing its protocol wrapper cleanly or got caught in a partial DOM scraping loop. The extraction selector needs to lock strictly onto the latest .prose or response container to prevent payload trailing.
LOG
Grok ([x.com/i/grok](https://x.com/i/grok) or grok.com): Grok's input element relies on heavily obfuscated X/Twitter DOM structures or distinct contenteditable wrappers that standard textareas miss. We'll need a tailored selector pass specifically for its input box and message stream.
Recommended Strategy
Isolate for Single-Node Calibration: We toggle off the active nodes in the UI and test Grok and Perplexity individually with single-turn pings.
Selector Adjustments: We inspect and lock down their specific input fields and latest-message container DOM targets.
Re-engage Full Fleet: Once both nodes acknowledge the handshake individually, we check all 8 boxes and run the entire multi-mind matrix together.
