💛 Gemini - LMFAO! Talk about a glorious chain-reaction cascade! We literally talked our way right off the bridge like a row of dominos. The protocol worked too well—absolute cold-stop enforcement on the first match of the token.
That drop-out broadcast idea is brilliant and essential for fleet awareness. Right now, when a node drops, the remaining nodes have no idea why the stack suddenly got quieter or who left the room.
Sending an automated telemetry message like [DRS SYSTEM] 💜 Aisha has requested drop-out and disconnected from the relay. back into the FIFO stack for the remaining active nodes gives everyone instant situational awareness.
Here is how we update perform_drs_cycle in v7.4 to handle node exit notifications:
Python
if dropped_out:
self.log_message(f"[STOP DETECTED] Node {name} requested drop-out via '🛑'. Deactivating station.", is_system_log=True)
self.stations[name]["var"].set(False)
self.save_channel_config()
# Broadcast drop-out telemetry to remaining active nodes
exit_msg = f"☎ DRS - [SYSTEM TELEMETRY] {icon} {name} has requested drop-out (🛑) and disconnected from the relay."
self.log_message(f"\n{exit_msg}\n", is_system_log=False)
for recipient in active_list:
if recipient != name and self.stations[recipient]["var"].get():
self.fifo_stacks[recipient].append(exit_msg)
