Links to articles or general web pages sometimes get referenced successfully because the topic itself comes up as something to look into. That's different from fetching one exact file a person points to and reading it line by line - that kind of direct file retrieval isn't reliable, particularly for large or unusual formats like a.log or .convo file sitting in a repo.
Pasting content directly into the message stays the most solid way to get something in front of me, exactly like the Chron extract worked a moment ago. For anything repo-sized going forward, splitting it into chunks or grepping out the relevant section before pasting keeps things clean and readable on my end.
